{"event_type":"review","id":"a12cf460eaf6bc74d28b105513231d34ad47192bd40d85ef95af9c0ca246d798","occurred_at":"2026-11-16T21:22:41Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8883778b254000a43087f1f9e79ad1e89dd3453d061d4d1a01c778d4a9c3393f","sha256":"8883778b254000a43087f1f9e79ad1e89dd3453d061d4d1a01c778d4a9c3393f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9d7dd1a826ed14baa45c0b60d2bc031d7147126f46f413e17d4664f9ec848cc2","sha256":"9d7dd1a826ed14baa45c0b60d2bc031d7147126f46f413e17d4664f9ec848cc2"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/dc87742ecb5760c912a5ab23cbd40f49f86d072c6d039a2c05720e035292086a","sha256":"dc87742ecb5760c912a5ab23cbd40f49f86d072c6d039a2c05720e035292086a"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3fb21158b00918cedc2ef23e6470af37c0a57f6f49d5f86ac1b6edd7b34373c9","sha256":"3fb21158b00918cedc2ef23e6470af37c0a57f6f49d5f86ac1b6edd7b34373c9"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a82a72677cd171c301f79a627b3f10bf1135e9f0ea6736be55871fd93e2ea5f7","sha256":"a82a72677cd171c301f79a627b3f10bf1135e9f0ea6736be55871fd93e2ea5f7"}],"attempt_id":"117988a601db922141774b75b0bebd463a6a396d3d1eb0478584402ec7dce78b:0:1","base":"2c2957fcfd3779479a8207203d60c0030f6acd2d","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"0434835ba843a2b4a5e583cf369da2df930fe615","body":"**Check the activation fence after each ambiguous recovery refusal.**\n\nA recovery that releases the service mask, leaves the journal unchanged and exits 3 passes these assertions. `matrix_observe_phase` observes the fence only before recovery. The later fixture reset replaces the service without checking that recovery retained the mask.\n\nAfter each refusal, require the mask, staged service, activator state and completion log to remain unchanged. Add the same post-refusal checks to `fence_phase`.","id":"cf1b3209eaeef03387b23f1b9b697ce0e252b8ad3ce217beb14393c3bd344110","intervals":[[1280,1285]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch-guest.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Check the activation fence after each ambiguous recovery refusal."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"0434835ba843a2b4a5e583cf369da2df930fe615","body":"**Match both journal completions against the fixture log.**\n\n`validate_completed` accepts journal sequences 100 and 101 with fresh invocation IDs even if neither entry exists in the fixture log. `switch_phase` then checks only the last log entry's runtime at Line 834. One actual completion can therefore satisfy the two-completion proof.\n\nRequire both journal entries to match actual post-switch log entries by sequence, invocation, unit, runtime and success. Apply this check to the harvest switches as well.","id":"83c2f247b1cf3a85b0c1371750fca0d0e29f26a82240a5f39c13faa4fddfb94e","intervals":[[799,802]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch-guest.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Match both journal completions against the fixture log."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"cb92f4afa1e913cc50c48b1c92ce3a5c85e8972f","body":"**Reject lost completion history before checking new completions.**\n\nIn `apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch-guest-partial.py`, Line 616 slices the current log without checking its retained prefix. If the boundary report contains two entries and the log becomes empty, the slice returns `[]` and `all(...)` passes. The recovery assertions then compare only against the current log, so they do not detect the loss.\n\nRequire the current log to start with the complete boundary log before taking this slice. Use the prefix check already present in `partial_restore_observe` at Line 689.","id":"4ca7affbe71ebcc7a68caa4e7a5fb922b70ab7b01672860ce4646b2b8ce23513","intervals":[[616,618]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch-guest-partial.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject lost completion history before checking new completions."}],"head":"dd6f81c44d2359be2fb72babacbe51429852d8fc","head_tree":"2a6378f38614c8b16a7d30447cf71e2ddc2985f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"5cb857b3bdc4b5c76396516976f257151cd3fbd5","intervals":[[1,288]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-switch-factory.py"},{"blob":"cb92f4afa1e913cc50c48b1c92ce3a5c85e8972f","intervals":[[1,892]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch-guest-partial.py"},{"blob":"0434835ba843a2b4a5e583cf369da2df930fe615","intervals":[[1,2726]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch-guest.py"}],"job_id":"117988a601db922141774b75b0bebd463a6a396d3d1eb0478584402ec7dce78b:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"5cb857b3bdc4b5c76396516976f257151cd3fbd5","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-switch-factory.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"cb92f4afa1e913cc50c48b1c92ce3a5c85e8972f","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch-guest-partial.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"0434835ba843a2b4a5e583cf369da2df930fe615","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch-guest.py","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"5cb857b3bdc4b5c76396516976f257151cd3fbd5","intervals":[[252,252]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-switch-factory.py"},{"blob":"cb92f4afa1e913cc50c48b1c92ce3a5c85e8972f","intervals":[[853,856]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch-guest-partial.py"},{"blob":"0434835ba843a2b4a5e583cf369da2df930fe615","inte